<title>USA: First Banks America Inc Q1 net decreases.</title>
<headline>First Banks America Inc Q1 net decreases.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months Ended</p>
<p>								 March 31,</p>
<p> Condensed Consolidated Statement of Income  1997	  1996</p>
<p> Net Interest Income			   $3,540	  $2,534</p>
<p> Provision for loan losses			550	     100</p>
<p> Net income (loss)				  377	     461</p>
<p> Net income (loss) per share		    .10	     .12</p>
<p>Weighted average common shares and</p>
<p>  common share equivalents outstanding    3,676	   4,008</p>
<p>Issued and outstanding shares:</p>
<p>   Common stock				   1,102	   1,315</p>
<p>   Class B common stock			 2,500	   2,500</p>
<p>		(In thousands, except net income/loss per share)</p>
<p>NOTE: The results for the first quarter of 1997 reflect the anticipated impact from the acquisition of Sunrise Bank which was completed on November 1, 1996.</p>
<p>Net income for the first quarter of 1997 includes $276,000 of interest expense attributable to the borrowings incurred in connection with funding the Sunrise Bank acquisition.</p>
</text>
